WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.449
A 6M-parameter model

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.298
that copies your

00:00:03.109 --> 00:00:03.923
handwriting

00:00:04.446 --> 00:00:05.908
Sam Greydanus built

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:06.757
PenGPT

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:08.007
a 6 million

00:00:07.819 --> 00:00:09.257
parameter transformer

00:00:09.069 --> 00:00:10.212
that writes print

00:00:10.071 --> 00:00:10.908
and cursive

00:00:11.062 --> 00:00:12.087
and imitates a

00:00:11.899 --> 00:00:13.042
new writer from

00:00:12.854 --> 00:00:13.726
just a few

00:00:13.538 --> 00:00:14.493
of their words

00:00:15.022 --> 00:00:15.882
A second

00:00:15.965 --> 00:00:17.616
54 million parameter

00:00:17.428 --> 00:00:18.842
model draws sketches

00:00:18.654 --> 00:00:19.880
from text prompts

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:21.045
Both share one

00:00:20.856 --> 00:00:22.247
tokenizer that turns

00:00:22.059 --> 00:00:23.203
pen strokes into

00:00:23.014 --> 00:00:23.887
moves in eight

00:00:23.698 --> 00:00:24.547
directions

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:26.261
The handwriting data

00:00:26.072 --> 00:00:29.669
covered 495,590 words

00:00:29.492 --> 00:00:32.216
by 1,255 writers

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:33.218
and the author

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:33.843
says the work

00:00:33.655 --> 00:00:35.140
was 80 percent data

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:36.684
Full story on

00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:37.391
the dashboard
